{
  "_note": "Full RFC 9421 proof-of-possession SIGNING vectors for the bound-retrieval GET (ADR-013 D1/D3), under the Web Bot Auth profile: the proof covers at least @method, @target-uri and the agent's Signature-Agent member, and carries tag=\"web-bot-auth\". The vectors array is the protocol SDK's own generated corpus, sdk/go/helpers/testdata/pop-vectors.json in module github.com/FORA-Protocol/protocol, copied whole: every vector, every field. The module's generator is the emitter and drift gate, and the SDK is the source of truth: refresh the array from there at every re-pin rather than editing values by hand; scripts/check-sdk-pin-consistency.sh fails a re-pin whose copy differs. Copied rather than read from the module cache because testdata cannot cross a module boundary (go:embed will not reach it) and a cache read breaks in vendored or air-gapped CI; testdata/thumbprint-vectors.json is the same arrangement. internal/testutil/edgedouble_test.go reads this file: it signs every vector in the form the SDK mints through the module and compares the emitted headers, and it replays every vector through the enforcing edge double, which must accept exactly the vectors marked expected_valid. expected_reason is the SDK verifier's refusal token; the double orders its checks independently, so its own token may differ and only the verdict is compared. presented_key_b64url is the X-FORA-Agent-Key value (base64url-no-pad raw 32-byte public key), signature_agent, signature_input and signature are the header values verbatim, and signature is STANDARD base64 inside the byte-string colons while the key is base64url. signer_seed_hex is the RFC 8032 seed the private key is derived from; agent_directory and nonce are the signer's inputs. now_unix is the verifier clock each expected_valid verdict holds at.",
